# Everything Claude keeps here is local to one machine and one session, EXCEPT
# the skills: those are how the project's own workflows are written down (see
# .claude/skills/app-mark), they reference this repo's files by path, and they
# are no more machine-local than DESIGN.md is.
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/

# EVERYTHING IN bin/ STAYS LOCAL. The compiled helpers (bs-pty, bs-ls) are
# ELF for one architecture and would be wrong on any other machine that
# cloned this, so they are built rather than committed: `banditshell build`.
# The CLI script beside them is machine state too - it is edited in place
# here and must never again hold a pull hostage with "local changes would be
# overwritten". Its SOURCE is tracked at cli/banditshell, and install.sh
# copies that into bin/ (again whenever cli/ is newer, so a pull updates the
# copy on the next install). The browser says the helpers are missing rather
# than failing quietly.
bin/

# Python bytecode, from running the scripts/ helpers directly.
__pycache__/
